    <string name="info_current_build_title">About the app</string>
    <string name="info_current_build_body">TgWsProxy for Android runs a local SOCKS5 proxy for Telegram and routes supported MTProto traffic through WebSocket connections.</string>
    <string name="info_mobile_body">Current mobile network tests show a working path only through CF Proxy. If direct Telegram routes are blocked, use CF only: supported traffic will go through the configured Cloudflare domain instead of direct Telegram upstreams.</string>
    <string name="info_cfproxy_body">Cloudflare Proxy is an alternative free route for unavailable Telegram data centers. TgWsProxy uses WebSocket hosts in the form kws*.domain, where the default domain is taken from the Flowseal/tg-ws-proxy project.</string>
    <string name="info_custom_domain_body">The default domain is intended as a ready-to-test option. For regular use, replace it with your own Cloudflare domain because shared Cloudflare WebSocket limits can make the default endpoint unavailable.</string>
    <string name="info_attribution_body">This app is based on the Android fork by amurcanov and runtime ideas/code from Flowseal tg-ws-proxy. The original projects and license notes are kept in the repository.</string>
    <string name="info_usage_body">Start the proxy, then tap \"Apply in Telegram\". For diagnostics, enable logs temporarily and save them to the selected report folder.</string>
