    <string name="onboarding_page1">TgWsProxy creates a local SOCKS5 proxy for Telegram and routes connections through Direct, Cloudflare Worker or CF proxy.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_page2">In Telegram, set SOCKS5:\nHost: 127.0.0.1\nPort: 1081\nNo username or password</string>
    <string name="onboarding_page3">Worker is a free fallback route through your own Cloudflare Worker.\nPaste only a domain like example.username.workers.dev</string>
    <string name="onboarding_page4">Auto is recommended.\nWorker first — if Direct fails often.\nCF first — if you have a working CF domain.\nWorker only / CF only — strict modes.\nDirect only — for tests.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_page5">The foreground notification shows proxy status. You can stop or reconnect from the notification. Android requires this notification while the proxy service is running.</string>
